# Everything is ignored by default; only the four entries below are tracked.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/data/
!/src/


# Python build products inside the two tracked trees
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub refuses any single file larger than 100 MB. The seven files below are
# over it, so a push containing them is rejected outright.
#
# None of them is a result. Each is either a raw download or an array rebuilt
# from one, and the script that produces it is committed, so the whole tree
# regenerates from src/ with no manual steps:
#
#   data/hydro/grace_obp.nc           886 MB   src/hydro/grace_hydro2.py
#   data/hydro/grace_tws.nc           507 MB   src/hydro/grace_hydro2.py
#   data/thermal/olr.day.mean.nc      333 MB   src/thermal/fetch_olr.py
#   data/ionosphere/tec_daily.npy     183 MB   src/ionosphere/fetch_tec.py
#   data/thermal/surf_air_cells.npy   149 MB   src/thermal/fetch_surface.py
#   data/thermal/surf_pwat_cells.npy  143 MB   src/thermal/fetch_surface.py
#   data/thermal/olr_cells.npy        129 MB   src/thermal/fetch_olr.py
#
# To distribute the binaries themselves, use Git LFS or deposit them with a DOI
# and cite that instead. Everything else under data/ and src/ is committed.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/hydro/grace_obp.nc
data/hydro/grace_tws.nc
data/thermal/olr.day.mean.nc
data/ionosphere/tec_daily.npy
data/thermal/surf_air_cells.npy
data/thermal/surf_pwat_cells.npy
data/thermal/olr_cells.npy
